# Security & Secrets

Follow `.rules/security-secrets.md` (canonical). Summary:

- Secrets (OPENROUTER_API_KEY, TWILIO_API_KEY, SENDGRID_API_KEY, OPENMEMORY_API_KEY, ...)
  exist ONLY as Windows environment variables and are read from the inherited environment
  at runtime.
- Never write secret values to files, configs, code, logs, prompts, tests, or memory.
  Reference variable names only.
- Missing variable → report `<VAR> missing from environment` and stop that integration.
